# tr909 — the SAME snare at two velocities, for the §J9 velocity→noisiness A/B (plan item 1.3).
# The 909 twin of tools/clips/tr808/02-snare-soft-vs-accent.script; same idea, different presets.
#
# Both cases come from the cart's own preset data, so nothing is hand-edited:
#   THE BELLS (1)  accent "x.......x......."  ·  SD "....x.......x..."   → snares NEVER accented (boost 0)
#   GABBER    (5)  accent "x...x...x...x..."  ·  SD "....x.......d..."   → snares ALWAYS accented (boost 2)
# Boot is GOOD LIFE (0), which has no snare row at all, so this steps RIGHT once to THE BELLS, holds, then
# RIGHT four more times to GABBER.
#
# Self-verifying, which is the point: the THE BELLS region must come out BYTE-IDENTICAL between
# tr909_snare_dyn=0 and =1 (soft hits are untouched by design), while the GABBER region must differ.
#   node tools/ab-render.js tr909 --file runtime/tr909.h --set tr909_snare_dyn=0,1 \
#        --script tools/clips/tr909/01-snare-soft-vs-accent.script --frames 400
# Snare slots for a stem render are TR9S_SDB/TR9S_SDN — check the cart's base before passing --solo-slot.
#
# Note GABBER's second snare is a 'd' (drag: two grace notes), a stroke the 909 cart owns; the plain 'x'
# on step 4 is the clean one to measure.
down 10 RIGHT
up 12 RIGHT
down 190 RIGHT
up 192 RIGHT
down 196 RIGHT
up 198 RIGHT
down 202 RIGHT
up 204 RIGHT
down 208 RIGHT
up 210 RIGHT
